  "result": "I've finished checking the archive and found the matching tickets, so I'm sending the answer now.\n\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46738\", \"PowerToys#4969\", \"PowerToys#23249\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#46738 asks for the same thing: hold Shift while dragging, then press Alt to cycle to the next saved FancyZones layout. It was made the main ticket for quick layout switching. PowerToys#4969 (scroll wheel) and PowerToys#23249 (non-primary mouse button) were closed as duplicates of it. The archive shows no implemented Alt-to-switch feature, so it isn't available yet. Add your use case or a thumbs-up to #46738. For now, you can assign a number to each custom layout in the FancyZones editor and switch layouts with Win+Ctrl+Alt+<number>. PowerToys#35058 shows a top-of-screen layout picker that appears while you drag with Shift held. The scripted workarounds in #4969 use AutoHotkey.\"}",
